  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 209 PM MDT TUE OCT 13 2026\nWarm and dry conditions will \nend the week with high pressure aloft over the Great Basin; this \nwill keep temperatures at 5-10 degrees above normal. A shortwave and \nassociated weak cold front on Sunday will help drop temperatures a \nfew degrees, although still in that above normal range. By mid-week \nnext week, there is good agreement on another trough digging down \nfrom the Gulf of Alaska into the western CONUS. this system will \nbring a more significant cool down and widespread precipitation \nchances. Below normal temperatures are favored again come Tuesday.",
